Sval: the content classifier's Remote Settings client stops notifying a shut-down service

Backport of Mozilla's Bug 2080226 (mozilla-central f3693da86126, Firefox
161), unchanged. ESR 153 does not carry it.
ContentClassifierRemoteSettingsClient's importAllLists and onSync captured
the service before their awaits, so a shutdown() during rs.get() or
deleteDownloaded() still called onListsChanged on it, which rejects with
NS_ERROR_NOT_INITIALIZED once ContentClassifierService::BlockShutdown has
run, and the rejection went uncaught. Both re-read the service after their
awaits. Its test is test_rs_client_shutdown.js.
Drop this patch when the upstream pin reaches Firefox 161.

